WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.280
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.190
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.940
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.640
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.730
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.100
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:43.040
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:49.280
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:56.550
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:03.300
What is truly precious?

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.820
Toon Summoned Skull?

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.040
As long as Toon World is on his field, my normal attacks won't work.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.160
And I also can't defend.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:30.400
In this situation, is there any way I can win?

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.520
No!

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.070
There is no way you can defeat me.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:42.080
If I give up, their three souls will never return.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.460
No matter how bad my odds are for winning, I can't afford to give up.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.720
That's pointless, Yugi boy.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.890
No matter how hard you try, it's over for you.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:02:00.900
Begin Counterattack!
Mind Shuffle

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.850
Dark Magician in attack position!

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.960
And Magical Hats!

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:41.540
This Dark Magician-Magical Hats combo may throw off Pegasus's attack.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.180
I see.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:52.580
You're stalling until you can find a way to overcome Toon World, but that's pointless.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:03:01.260
Yugi boy, you decide which hat Dark Magician hides under.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:05.730
That means I also know which hat it's hiding in.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:20.400
Dark Magician is hiding under the leftmost hat.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.080
He read my thoughts.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.950
Are you ready, Yugi boy?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.600
Even my Magical Hats combo doesn't work.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.900
I can't find a way to defeat the power of Pegasus's Millennium Eye!

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.330
Yugi, don't give up!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.100
Yugi, don't lose!

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:52.040
Toon Summoned Skull, attack Magical Hat!

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.530
Dark Magician is destroyed.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.350
Why?

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:21.770
Dark Magician's data hasn't been erased, and the card is still on the field!

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.950
Unbelievable!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:27.710
Dark Magician is hiding under a different hat?

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.300
Impossible.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.520
I clearly read Yugi boy's mind.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:37.550
I moved Dark Magician to hide it under a different Magical Hat.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.190
It seems you couldn't read my other mind.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.630
You're Yugi boy's other mind!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.600
That's...

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.360
Anzu, what does he mean by another mind?

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.940
It's his other soul.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:00.880
Yugi once told me that there's another version of himself inside him.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.220
What's going on, Yugi?

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:11.420
I haven't told anyone, but when I'm dueling, I'm not my usual self.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:18.700
I switch places with my other self that lives inside my heart, and he duels.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.230
And I watch from the depths of my heart.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:30.170
But when I saw my other self suffering in this duel, I couldn't just stand back and do nothing.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:34.020
Even my Magical Hats combo doesn't work.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:39.420
I can't find a way to defeat the power of Pegasus's Millennium Eye!

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.900
My other self...

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.050
Please hear my voice.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.190
My other self...

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:57.650
What's this voice that I can hear from inside my heart?

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:00.280
My other self!

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.860
He's calling me.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.280
My other self!

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.390
You heard my voice!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.840
Yeah.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:27.120
This is the first time we're meeting inside our heart and I'm talking to you.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:32.500
No matter how loud I shouted, my voice never reached you.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:39.640
Even though I knew you were suffering in battle, there was nothing I could do.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.880
But I finally reached you!

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.950
Why did you call me?

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.200
Please let me duel too.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.820
You can't face Pegasus's power alone!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:58.600
But I can't find a way to overcome his Millennium Eye.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:08.070
Pegasus can read your mind, but maybe he can't read mine!

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:10.550
I see.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:17.380
If Pegasus can only read one mind, if we face him with two minds...

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:23.100
Will you lend me your strength?

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.300
This may be hard to believe...

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:40.000
...but since the day I solved this Puzzle, I've been switching back and forth with my other self.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:50.580
I think I transform into a different version sometimes.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.080
Don't worry about that.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.400
You'll always be Yugi.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:06.130
So when he was talking about another version, he wasn't talking about an emotional change.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.800
Another personality takes over?

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.170
He has a split personality?  Am I right?

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.540
It's my turn.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:22.080
I set this card and end my turn.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:27.220
Pegasus, do you know what card I drew and set?

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.250
Try and read my mind.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.350
Then you'll know, right?

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.260
Of course.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:38.640
Mind Scan!

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:51.070
Why?

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:54.140
I can't see the image of the set card!

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.460
Unfortunately, I don't know the identity of this set card either.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.320
It's pointless to read my mind, Pegasus!

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:05.250
He switched minds again?

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:12.950
Pegasus, it seems you need time to read someone's mind with your Millennium Eye.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:17.050
While you were doing that, I switched my mind with my other self.

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:21.700
We've solved your Millennium Eye using Mind Shuffle!

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.640
Mind Shuffle?

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:27.760
I see.  Yugi is battling with two minds.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:33.450
Even if Pegasus can read one of his minds, Yugi can fight back with the other one!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.450
Yeah!  This will work!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.180
You can't escape!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.120
Let's play a game.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:00.910
If your weapons are those hunks of steel, my weapons are these cards.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.940
Stop joking!

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:03.850
Give up!

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:10.100
I've seen that look on his face before.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:20.130
It's the other Bakura from before.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.340
It wasn't a dream after all.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.070
It's my turn.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.270
Man-Eater Bug.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.310
What's this?

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:02.520
What is that?

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.700
You monster!

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:22.020
Your turns are over.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:23.700
What was that?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.960
How did it become real without a Duel System?

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:31.120
It's my turn.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.180
I'll save you from Man-Eater Bug.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:53.700
But your situation may have gotten worse.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.780
Who is he?

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:04.960
Where are we?

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.840
It's your turn, Pegasus.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:17.880
Unbelievable.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:23.150
I don't know which hat Dark Magician is hiding under nor the identity of his set card.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:27.450
They're hidden in the other Yugi boy's mind.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:39.700
But as long as I have Toon World on my field, your monsters can't attack me.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:47.140
Your only option is to keep your Dark Magician hidden in those Magical Hats for three more turns.

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:53.580
Then Pegasus, try to pick Dark Magician among these hats.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:13:00.250
Or are you a coward who can't make his own decisions without his Millennium Eye?

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:07.700
Now that you mention it, I haven't relied on my own instincts for some years now.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.830
Toon Summoned Skull!

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.120
No!  I missed again!

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.880
Too bad.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.580
You missed again.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:47.830
Pegasus, as the creator of Duel Monsters, you know that a game divides winners from losers.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.660
So how is the line drawn?

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:56.480
It's with the ability to make decisions that give you control of the game.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:14:00.410
And an all-or-nothing instinct.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.420
Whoever does this better will win.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:09.660
Decision making comes from experience and confidence, but instinct requires courage.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:17.260
Since you relied too much on the power of the Millennium Eye, you lost the instincts you need as a duelist.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:22.930
My partner has many times more courage than you.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:26.130
Here I go!

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.220
He switched minds again.

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:33.910
It's my turn.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.720
This card looks useful.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:46.060
I set this card and end my turn!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.630
It's your turn.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.630
A second set card.

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:57.000
I don't know its identity either.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:01.570
I don't know what these two set cards are either.

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:08.400
But I believe in the cards that my other self selected!

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.640
My turn.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.460
Great!

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:22.900
My card is Magical Neutralizing Force Field!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:26.370
I activate this card on your field!

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:37.110
This card eliminates all active spell effects on your field.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:41.940
That means Magical Hats' spell effect vanishes!

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:47.780
Oh no!  Dark Magician is revealed!

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.660
This is the end, Yugi boy.

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:58.300
A great duelist doesn't need instincts.

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:03.240
He thinks about how to win without taking any risks.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.530
Come out, Toon Summoned Skull!

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:15.960
Only Toons can destroy Toon Monsters.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:20.250
Toon Summoned Skull's attack will destroy Dark Magician.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:24.340
Toon Summoned Skull, attack Dark Magician!

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:34.630
Now!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.770
It's the other Yugi!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.960
I flip over my set card!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.510
Spell Shattering Arrow!

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.380
What?  Spell Shattering Arrow?

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:57.870
Pegasus, you didn't notice that my role was to play the card, and my other self was to provoke you.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:58.820
What?

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:06.500
Since you lost your cool, you played a card that would remove Magical Hats' effect from the field.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:11.400
But that was our goal.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:15.510
Because we also want to remove a spell's effect from the field.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:21.680
Pegasus, we use Spell Shattering Arrow to send Magical Neutralizing Force Field back to you!

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:29.640
But it's too late.

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:33.260
You can't stop Toon Summoned Skull's attack.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.660
Dark Magician is destroyed.

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.080
Too bad.

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.850
The other card I set was...

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:48.740
The trap card Mirror Force.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.180
A trap?

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:58.450
Magical Neutralizing Force Field destroys Toon World!

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:02.900
Your Toon Monsters appear on the field in their original forms.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.490
No!

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:15.070
Unbelievable!  My beloved monsters!

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:18.740
This is a nightmare!  A bad dream!

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:22.010
No!  This can't really be happening!

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.320
We did it!

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:26.950
All the Toons are destroyed!

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:30.880
Yes.  It was your courage that destroyed the Toons.

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:41.560
I never thought that Yugi boy's two minds would stop my Mind Scan!

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:44.500
All right!  You did it, Yugi!

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:46.260
Yugi!

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:50.100
By combining your two hearts, you can defeat Pegasus!

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:53.110
He can save Grandpa and the others!

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.620
What's going on?

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.760
What's happening?

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:10.620
I remember now, Bakura.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.660
It wasn't a dream.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.240
You're not Bakura!

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:19.760
You're another Bakura that has taken over his soul!

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:23.960
It would've been better if you didn't remembered that.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.700
Hand over Mokuba.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:28.040
I won't hand him over to you!

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:32.080
Do you also want to fall victim to the power of the shadows?

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:33.980
Powers of the shadows?

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:46.560
Wonderful.

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:52.560
No wonder you deserve to possess a Millennium Item.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:55.770
I can't play around anymore.

00:19:56.460 --> 00:20:03.540
I must duel with the greatest honor and strategies.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:11.620
Yugi boy, it will now be a battle between those chosen by the Millennium Items.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:15.420
We will decide this in a Shadow Game!

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:16.920
A Shadow Game?

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:38.900
An eerie darkness surrounds Yugi and Pegasus.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.040
This is a Shadow Game!

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.900
I can't believe it, but it's not a dream!

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:48.750
What is happening inside the darkness?

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:54.600
We can feel that Yugi is in agony, but we can't do anything to help!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:57.950
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Evil Eye Activates
Relinquished

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.600
Duel, standby!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:12.350
The flask glistens

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:20.200
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:29.180
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:36.950
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:42.780
Shower of happiness

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:46.890
I will shower you with it

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:55.170
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:59.410
Shower of happiness

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:03.530
You are not alone

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:10.250
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
